{"raw": {"https://apply.interfolio.com/190337": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Psychology Location: St. Mary's City, MD The Department of Psychology at St. Mary's College of Maryland is accepting applications for the tenure track position of Assistant Professor of Psychology (Clinical/Counseling), beginning fall 2027. An interest in attracting and retaining students from underrepresented groups is essential. The salary range for this position is $65,000 to $78,000 based on level of experience; startup costs are negotiable; benefits information is available online ( https://www.smcm.edu/human-resources/benefits-and-leave/ ). Teaching responsibilities will include general courses in the psychology major (e.g., Intro to Psychology; Psychological Research, Analysis, and Writing; Scientific Writing and Professional Development), breadth courses in Clincal/Counseling, and topics courses in an area of specialization. The standard teaching load is 3 courses per semester, although supervision of senior thesis projects counts toward the teaching load. The development of an active research program involving undergraduates is expected, and a commitment to culturally competent teaching/mentoring and fostering inclusive and equitable learning environments is essential. St. Mary's College is committed to excellence in teaching and undergraduate research. To support your transition and professional development, first-year faculty are provided a reduced workload, shared course materials, and a structured mentoring program. We offer negotiated start-up grants and lab space to continue your research, especially encouraging projects that involve undergraduate students. Opportunities to include students in research are rewarded through guided research courses, such as PSYC 396 - Collaborative Research and PSYC X97 - Directed Research. The department has a robust history of bringing student and faculty research to regional and national conferences, and a number of faculty have collaborated with students on peer-reviewed publications ( https://www.smcm.edu/program-psychology/research-opportunities/ ). The department values theoretical, empirical, and applied scholarship; there are many ways to thrive as a professor here. Non-sectarian since its founding, St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland, a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C., has been designated a national public honors college. With selective admissions policies, academically talented students, and a rigorous curriculum, we offer a small college experience similar to that found at exceptional private colleges. St. Mary\u2019s faculty benefit from a comprehensive program of support for scholarship, research, travel, and curriculum development, including course releases for pre\u00adtenure faculty and leaves for tenured faculty. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and by our proximity to Washington, D.C. and Baltimore. Applicants must have a Ph.D. in Psychology or a related field (ABD acceptable at the time of application). Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College is committed to access, equity, inclusion, and diversity. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences, and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. The Psychology Department seeks scholars whose pedagogical practice improves the educational experience of underrepresented students. Preference will be given to candidates with a proven commitment to culturally responsive teaching practices that promote belonging, inclusion, and equity. Application materials should include a cover letter (which should speak to ways in which the candidate's teaching will contribute to a campus culture of inclusion), curriculum vitae (including email address), statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research interests, and evidence of teaching effectiveness if available (e.g., teaching evaluations, observation notes). We request three professional references (rather than letters of recommendation) at the time of application. Of these three references, at least one referee should speak to the candidate's disciplinary expertise, and at least one should have seen the candidate deliver or design classroom instruction. References will be contacted only for candidates who advance to finalist interviews. Applications are being accepted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/190337 , with reviews starting on September 1, 2026 and continuing until the position is filled. Applicants should expect a response by October 15, 2026. Questions may be directed to Scott Mirabile at spmirabile@smcm.edu."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/190488": {"title": "Assistant Professor and Internship Coordinator in Counseling and Clinical Psychology", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Psychology Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary's College of Maryland is accepting applications for the tenure track position of Assistant Professor and Internship Coordinator in its newly approved Masters of Arts in Counseling and Clinical Psychology (MACCP) program, beginning August 2027. The MACCP program is the second Masters program at SMCM (following the successful Master of Teaching program). The salary range for this position is $75,000 to $79,000 based on level of experience; startup costs are negotiable; benefits information is available online ( https://www.smcm.edu/human-resources/benefits-and-leave/ ). The standard teaching load is 12 credits (usually, the equivalent of 3 courses) per semester. The internship Coordinator will be in charge of preparing for internship placements (which is\u00a0 built into the teaching load). Teaching responsibilities will include courses in the Master of Arts in Counseling and Clinical Psychology program (e.g., Psychopathology and Diagnosis, Multicultural Counseling, Lifespan Development, Group Counseling, Psychological Testing, Family Systems in Practice), as well as the possibility of undergraduate courses in your area of specialization to provide cross-program collaboration with the Psychology major. At SMCM, we seek faculty whose pedagogical practice involves culturally responsive teaching practices that promote belonging and inclusion. New faculty are paired with mentors to support your growth as a teacher-scholar. In addition, we offer start-up funding to support your research, especially encouraging projects that relate to the training of psychotherapy practitioners. Over time, professors take on roles in services to the program and College to support the College's mission; first-year faculty are exempt from college-wide committee work. Non-sectarian since its founding, St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland, a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C., has been designated a national public honors college. With selective admissions policies, academically talented students, and a rigorous curriculum, we offer a small college experience similar to that found at exceptional private colleges. St. Mary\u2019s faculty benefit from a comprehensive program of support for scholarship, research, travel, and curriculum development, including course releases for pre\u00adtenure faculty and leaves for tenured faculty. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and by our proximity to Washington, D.C. and Baltimore. Ph.D. in Counseling or Clinical Psychology or related field (ABD acceptable at the time of application) Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include a cover letter (which should speak to ways in which the candidate's teaching will contribute to the training of Masters students in counseling and clinical psychology), curriculum vitae (including email address), statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research interests, and evidence of teaching effectiveness if available (e.g., teaching evaluations, observation notes). We request three professional references (rather than letters of recommendation) at the time of application. Of these three references, at least one referee should speak to the candidate's disciplinary expertise, and at least one should have seen the candidate deliver or design classroom instruction. References will be contacted only for candidates who advance to finalist interviews. Applications are being accepted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/190488 , with reviews starting September 1, 2026 and continuing until the position is filled. Questions may be directed to Dr. Libby Nutt Williams at enwilliams@smcm.edu ."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/190323": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Developmental Biology/Cell Biology", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Biology Location: St. Mary's City, MD The Department of Biology at St. Mary's College of Maryland is accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Developmental Biology , beginning August 2027. Teaching responsibilities will include participation in one or more of our core biology courses (Principles of Biology I and II, Genetics, and Ecology and Evolution), an upper division laboratory course in developmental biology and/or cell biology and further opportunities to teach electives and biology laboratories in the candidate's specialty. It would be a strong asset if the candidate is also able to teach an upper division course in human anatomy. There is also the expectation that the successful candidate will establish and maintain an exceptional research program involving undergraduates. All professors at St. Mary's College are expected to contribute to the college-wide core curriculum as well as to their departmental curriculum. The salary range for this position is $80,000 to $83,000, depending on qualifications and experience. The Department of Biology faculty are committed to creating a respectful community of educators and scholars and seek colleagues who are eager to nurture and support growth of students, staff, and faculty, including BIPOC, LGBTQ+, first generation and international community members, as well as community members with disabilities, among others. This position is being filled as part of our Life at the Molecular and Cellular Scale cluster hire initiative. The candidate hired in this role will be part of a five-member cluster that will meet regularly to build community across programs that teach chemistry and biology at the molecular/cellular level, develop cross-disciplinary research collaborations, work together to develop an integrated inquiry general education pathway attractive to STEM majors, and build new partnerships with community organizations that will provide experiential learning opportunities for our majors. The candidate will have regular contact with a steering committee composed of faculty and staff from offices across campus and will receive additional professional development support to encourage retention and successful completion of the cluster mission. This support includes an additional course release pre-tenure (leading to a total of three pre-tenure course releases), support to attend an off-campus leadership development opportunity, guaranteed support for one summer research student each of the first two years, assistance in planning a five-year professional success arc, grant planning and preparation support, community onboarding, and training in governance and pedagogy. Non-sectarian since its founding, St. Mary's College of Maryland, a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C., has been designated as Maryland's public honors college. With selective admissions policies, academically talented students, and a rigorous curriculum, we offer a small college experience similar to that found at exceptional private colleges. St. Mary's faculty benefit from a comprehensive program of support for scholarship, research, travel, and curriculum development, including course releases for pre-tenure faculty and leaves for tenured faculty. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and by our proximity to Washington, D.C. and Baltimore. Applicants must have a Ph.D. in biology or related fields and be committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary's College of Maryland embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include a cover letter (within the cover letter, applicants are requested to speak to ways in which their teaching will contribute to a culture of inclusion and campus diversity), curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research interests including plan for seeking external funding, and evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available). In support of inclusive hiring practices, the College will also request three professional references (rather than letters of recommendation) at the time of application. Of these three references, at least one referee should speak to the candidate's disciplinary expertise and at least one should have seen the candidate deliver or design classroom instruction. References will be contacted only for candidates who advance to finalist interviews. Applications are being accepted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/190323 . Questions may be directed to Dr. Emily Brownlee. Department Chair, at efbrownlee@smcm.edu. Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/190332": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Economics", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Economics Location: St. Mary's City, MD The Department of Economics and Business at St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland is accepting applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Economics with a specialization in Empirical Economics to support the College's Data Science minor, beginning August 2027. This position will regularly teach both Economics and Data Science courses and is open to any subfield within Economics, with priority given to candidates with empirical, policy-oriented research and experience. Faculty members teach three courses per semester, advise program majors, supervise senior projects, and fulfill departmental and college-level service responsibilities. All professors at St. Mary's are expected to contribute to the college-wide core curriculum as well as to their departmental curriculum. Faculty are expected to teach in-person classes supported on methodologies that promote students' engagement. The annual salary range for this position is $85,000 to $100,000, commensurate with the candidate's qualifications and experience. Non-sectarian since its founding, St. Mary's College of Maryland, a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C., has been designated as Maryland's public honors college. With selective admissions policies, academically talented students, and a rigorous curriculum, we offer a small college experience similar to that found at exceptional private colleges. St. Mary\u2019s faculty benefit from a comprehensive program of support for scholarship, research, travel, and curriculum development, including course releases for pre-tenure faculty and leaves for tenured faculty. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and by our proximity to Washington, D.C. and Baltimore. Ph.D. in Economics (may be ABD at time of application if degree completion by August 2027 is certain), with a record of high-quality teaching and research. Must have college-level teaching experience, and a record of\u2014or demonstrating promise of\u2014high quality intellectual contributions. Candidates must be able to design and deliver courses in Economics and Data Science, and must be proficient in the programming languages R and Python. Preference will be given to candidates with teaching, research, or applied experience in empirical, policy-oriented economics, including data scraping, data visualization, or machine learning. An interest in attracting and retaining students from underrepresented groups is desirable. The successful candidate must produce the necessary documentation to legally work in the U.S. upon hire. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College (www.smcm.edu) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include a cover letter (within the cover letter, applicants are requested to speak to ways in which their teaching will contribute to a culture of inclusion and campus diversity), curriculum vitae (include e-mail address), statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research interests, and evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available). In support of inclusive hiring practices, the College will also request three professional references (rather than letters of recommendation) at the time of application. Of these three references, at least one referee should speak to the candidate's disciplinary expertise and at least one should have seen the candidate deliver or design classroom instruction. References will be contacted only for candidates who advance to finalist interviews. Applications are being accepted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/190332 . Questions may be directed to Silvio Borrero at sborrero@smcm.edu. Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026 and continue until the positions are filled. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/190935": {"title": "Lecturer of Art History and Museum Studies", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Art and Art History Location: St. Mary's City, MD The Museum Studies Program and Department of Art at St. Mary's College of Maryland are accepting applications for the position of Lecturer of Art History and Museum Studies, beginning August 2027. The salary range for this position is $60,000 to $63,000, depending on qualifications and experience. Teaching responsibilities will include Survey in Art History (2-semester sequence), Contemporary Art, and Introduction to Museum Studies, as well as topics courses in Art History and Museum Studies based on the instructor's specialization. Additional responsibilities will include coordinating and supervising undergraduate internships in Museum Studies. All professors at St. Mary's are expected to contribute to the college-wide LEAD Curriculum, as well as to their departmental curriculum. Candidates whose course arrays can contribute to the LEAD Cultural Literacy requirement may be preferred. An interest in attracting and retaining students from underrepresented groups is desirable. Non-\u00adsectarian since its founding, St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland, a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C., has been designated as Maryland's public honors college.\u00a0 With selective admissions policies, academically talented students, and a rigorous curriculum, we offer a small college experience similar to that found at exceptional private colleges.\u00a0 The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and by our proximity to Washington, D.C. and Baltimore. Ph.D. in Art History or related field required. Commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching. Expertise in Contemporary and Modern Art History, Global & Non-Western Art History, American Art History, and/or Curatorial Practices or Exhibit Design preferred. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College is committed to access, equity, inclusion, and diversity. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences, and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include cover letter (within the cover letter, applicants are requested to speak to ways in which their teaching will contribute to a culture of inclusion and campus diversity), curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research interests, and evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available). I n support of inclusive hiring practices, for all SMCM faculty searches initiated after February 15, 2023, the College will also request three professional references (rather than letters of recommendation) at the time of application. Of these three references, a t least one referee should speak to the candidate's disciplinary expertise and at least one should have seen the candidate deliver or design classroom instruction. References will be contacted only for candidates who advance to finalist interviews. Applications are being accepted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/190935 . Questions may be directed to Dr. Sarah Malena at slmalena@smcm.edu. Review of applications will begin on September 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/193023": {"title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Philosophy", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Philosophy and Religious Studies Location: St. Mary's City, MD The Department of Philosophy at St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland is accepting applications for a 1.5 year position as a Visiting Assistant Professor of Philosophy for three (3) semesters, beginning January 2027 until May 2028. The salary range for this position is $63,700 to $71,000, depending on qualifications and experience. Non-sectarian since its founding, St. Mary's College of Maryland, a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C., has been designated as Maryland's public honors college. With selective admissions policies, academically talented students, and a rigorous curriculum, we offer a small college experience similar to that found at exceptional private colleges. St. Mary\u2019s faculty benefit from a comprehensive program of support for scholarship, research, travel, and curriculum development, including course releases for pre-tenure faculty and leaves for tenured faculty. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and by our proximity to Washington, D.C. and Baltimore. Applicants must have a Ph.D. in Philosophy and be committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching within a Liberal Arts setting. Areas of Specialization and Areas of Competence are open, but the department has specific teaching needs in Asian philosophy, early Modern philosophy, Logic, Introduction to Philosophy, Introduction to Ethics, the College\u2019s First-year Seminar, and upper-division Topics courses in the candidate\u2019s area of specialization. All professors at St. Mary\u2019s are expected to contribute to the college-wide core curriculum as well as to their departmental curriculum. An interest in attracting and retaining students from underrepresented groups is desirable. The successful candidate must produce the necessary documentation to legally work in the U.S. upon hire. The successful candidate must produce the necessary documentation to legally work in the U.S. upon hire. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College (www.smcm.edu) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include a cover letter (within the cover letter, applicants are requested to speak to ways in which their teaching will contribute to a culture of inclusion), curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research, and evidence of teaching effectiveness. In support of inclusive hiring practices, we request three professional references (rather than letters of recommendation) at the time of application. Of these three references, at least one referee should speak to the candidate's disciplinary expertise and at least one should have seen the candidate deliver or design classroom instruction. References will be contacted only for candidates who advance to finalist interviews. Applications are being accepted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/193023 . Questions may be directed to Dr. Bradley Park at bdpark@smcm.edu. Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/194035": {"title": "Lab Facilities Coordinator and Instructional Support Specialist", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Biology Location: St. Mary's City, MD 20686 The Department of Biology at St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland is accepting applications for the position of Lab Facilities Coordinator and Instructional Support Specialist. The salary range for this position is $55,000 to $60,000, depending on qualifications and experience. The anticipated start date is November 1, 2026. The responsibilities and duties of the Biology Facilities Coordinator and Instructional Support Specialist will be multifaceted and include coordinating instruction and design for the Principles of Biology first-year laboratory courses, acting as the coordinator for the Biology Teaching Assistants, and managing Biology outreach, events, and facilities. This position reports to the Biology department chair. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Applicants must have a Bachelor's or Master's degree in Biology or a related field. Candidates with Master's degrees are preferred. Preference will be given to candidates with experience in working with laboratory safety, with technical expertise in scientific equipment. Candidates are expected to have excellent oral and written communication skills, and proven attention to detail and organizational ability. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include a cover letter, resume and three professional references. References will be contacted only for candidates who advance to finalist interviews. Applications are being accepted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/194035 . Questions may be directed to Emily Brownlee at efbrownlee@smcm.edu. Review of resumes will begin immediately and continue until October 15, 2026. The anticipated start date for this position is November 1, 2026."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/195694": {"title": "Lab Coordinator and Instructional Support Specialist", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Environmental Studies Location: St. Mary's City, MD The Departments of Environmental Studies and Marine Science at St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland are accepting applications for the position of Lab Coordinator and Instructional Support Specialist, beginning December 1, 2026. The salary range is $55,000 to $60,000, depending on qualifications and experience. Qualifications: Applicants must have a Master\u2019s degree in Environmental Science, Marine Science, or a related field, or a Bachelor\u2019s degree with documented equivalent experience. Candidates with Master's degrees are preferred. Candidates must have the ability to work well with students and faculty in a small, liberal-arts college. Preference will be given to candidates with teaching experience or experience working with students. Preference is also given to candidates who have experience in working with laboratory safety, and with technical expertise in scientific lab equipment and scientific field equipment. Candidates are expected to have excellent oral and written communication skills, and proven attention to detail and organizational ability. The responsibilities and duties of the Lab Coordinator and Instructional Support Specialist will be multifaceted and include teaching six lab sections per year, managing inventory of lab supplies, maintaining laboratory resources and laboratory instructional materials, and other related duties. This position reports to the Dean of the North Division which houses the departments of Environmental Studies and Marine Science. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Master\u2019s degree in Environmental Science, Marine Science, or a related field, or a Bachelor\u2019s degree with documented equivalent experience. Candidates with Master's degrees are preferred. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary's College (www.smcm.edu) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences, and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should be submitted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/195694 and include: Cover Letter Resume Three (3) Professional References Questions may be directed to Sahar Shafqat, Dean, at sshafqat@smcm.edu. Review of resumes will begin October 30, 2026 and continue until the position is filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/193735": {"title": "Office Associate II in Accessibility Services", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Student Affairs Location: Saint Marys City, MD, United States St. Mary's College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary's City is accepting resumes for the position of Office Associate II/Office of Accessibility Services . The salary range for this position is $38,980 to $47,735, depending on qualifications and experience. Job Duties Performs complex duties such as, record keeping and administrative detail, and follow-up functions to assist the Director/Department Head and department staff in implementing departmental programs. May act as secretary to an academic division. Must be well organized and possess good secretarial skills. Receives minimal supervision and independently exercises considerable discretion and judgement in all work areas. May handle confidential and sensitive issues. May supervise other clerical employees and student employees. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Applicants must have a high school diploma or GED equivalent, Associates Degree preferred, with successful completion of courses in typing/word processing (minimum speed of 40wpm), data entry, Dbase, spreadsheets and microcomputer systems. At least five (5) years of full-time employment in the secretarial/administration field. Strong verbal and written communications skills, good organizational skills. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary's College (www.smcm.edu) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences, and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include a cover letter, resume (including e-mail address), and three references, and submitted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/193735 . Questions may be directed to Dr. Jerri Howland at 240-895-4208. Review of resumes will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/159675": {"title": "Digital Media Specialist", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Business and Finance: OIT Location: Saint Marys City, MD, United States St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary\u2019s City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for the position of Digital Media Specialist. This position is responsible for promoting and supporting digital media instruction and production in support of the college curriculum. The position includes responsibility for developing and maintaining the digital media lab and the recording studio; direct instruction of students, faculty, and staff; training and scheduling of student staff; and providing consultation services for campus users. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Bachelor\u2019s degree in media production or a related field preferred. Three years\u2019 experience in a media-related field (video and audio production, photography) and experience working, teaching, or training in an academic setting preferred. Demonstrated proficiency in audio and video production with extensive experience in Adobe Creative Cloud apps (including but not limited to: Premiere Pro, Photoshop and Illustrator) Final Cut Pro X, and Logic Pro X (or equivalent). Strong customer service orientation, interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills are desired. Supervisory skills and demonstrated ability to work independently. Possess a valid driver\u2019s license. Ability to lift approximately fifty (50) pounds. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. The annual salary is $60,000, depending on qualifications and experience. View position description . St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), and three references and submitted online at: apply.interfolio.com/159675 . Questions may be directed to Lisa Smith at lmsmith3@smcm.edu . Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer. Visit our website: www.smcm.edu/hr"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/171445": {"title": "Information Technology Support Technician", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Business and Finance: OIT Location: St. Mary's City, Maryland 20686 St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary\u2019s City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for the position of Information Technology Support Technician . \u00a0The Information Technology (IT) Support Technician is responsible for providing technical and computer services, training and assistance to the campus community. The IT Support Technician will work daily with computer hardware and software, repairing and replacing defective equipment, installing and testing new and/or upgraded software. IT Support Technicians will help troubleshoot problems with members of the campus community and are on-call during office hours to provide field support as needed for the user in need. \u00a0As the position requires constant interaction with the campus community, strong communication skills are essential. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. High School Diploma or equivalent; Associate\u2019s degree or above preferred. At least four years of recent relevant experience at troubleshooting both PC and MAC hardware and software problems. Ability to lift and move computers, monitors, and other hardware. Strong verbal, written and organizational skills including spelling, grammar and record maintenance procedures. Ability to handle sensitive situations. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. The salary range is $55,000 - $62,000, depending on qualifications and experience. View position description . St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity.\u00a0 Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), and three references and submitted online at: apply.interfolio.com/171445 . Questions may be directed to Jennifer Falkowski at jafalkowski@smcm.edu . Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer. Visit our website: www.smcm.edu/hr"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/192100": {"title": "Director of Desktop and User Support Services", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Business and Finance: OIT Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland is accepting applications for the position of Director of Desktop and User Support Services . This position directs the User Support Services unit in the Office of Information Technology (OIT). Responsibilities include the effective supervision and management of all User and Desktop Support Services staff and students; managing the OIT Support Center; managing the hardware and software assets of the College; managing all campus-wide server-based (web, email, enterprise applications) systems, data storage, backup and recovery processes, and advising the Associate Vice President of Information Technology and CIO in devising and promulgating policies and requirements for the proper and effective use of computing resources at the College. The salary range for this position is $94,000 to $104,000, depending on qualifications and experience. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Systems, Business Administration, or a related field. Seven (7) years of progressively responsible experience in information technology support, endpoint management, customer service operations, or related areas. Three (3) years of supervisory or management experience. Demonstrated experience managing enterprise endpoint environments, service management platforms, technology asset management programs, and customer support operations. Experience developing budgets, managing vendors, negotiating contracts, and leading technology projects. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education information technology environments. Experience with Microsoft 365, Google Workspace, endpoing management platforms, mobile device management solutions, and service management systems. ITIL, Microsoft, CompTIA, HDI, or related professional certifications. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), statement of how the applicant\u2019s employment at the College will contribute to a culture of inclusion and campus diversity, and three references and submitted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/192100 . Questions may be directed to E. Jenell Sargent at ejsargent@smcm.edu. Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/192104": {"title": "Systems Administrator/Senior Systems Administrator", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Business and Finance: OIT Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary\u2019s City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for the position of Systems Administrator/Senior Systems Administrator . This position is responsible for overseeing the administration of\u00a0 local area networks, campus-wide server-based (web, email, enterprise applications) systems, data storage, virtualization, backup and recovery processes.\u00a0 Additional responsibilities include: integrity and security of all server and appliance operating systems; designing and implementing server redundancy, survivability, protection, backup, and recovery systems; verifying continuing need for server hardware and software support agreements; determining the benefit versus risk of new software and hardware implementations; and conducting technical reviews of all special projects interfacing with or having a potential impact on university server-based applications. The salary range for this position is $79,000 to $82,000, depending on qualifications and experience. Non-sectarian since its founding, St. Mary's College of Maryland, a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C., has been designated as Maryland's public honors college.\u00a0 Undergraduate and residential in nature, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1700, St. Mary's emphasizes excellence in teaching.\u00a0 The institution was awarded a chapter of Phi Beta Kappa in 1997.\u00a0 The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Systems Administrator Associate's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field required; Bachelor's degree preferred. Equivalent combinations of education, training, and experience may be considered. Minimum of five (5) years of relevant experience in systems administration, endpoint engineering, infrastructure support, or related technical operations. Experience supporting Microsoft Windows and MacOS operating environments in an enterprise environment. Experience administering endpoing management and systems administration technologies. Experience supporting virtualization technologies, cloud services, or enterprise infrastructure preferred. Working knowledge of Microsoft Windows Server and desktop operating systems. Knowledge of Microsoft Active Directory, Microsoft Entra ID, Group Policy, and enterprise authentication services. Experience with endpoint management platforms such as Microsoft Intune, JAMF, MECM/SCCM, or equivalent technologies. Understanding of virtualization technologies and virtual desktop infrastructure (VDI). Knowledge of software deployment, patch management, operating system imaging, and endpoint security practices. Ability to troubleshoot complex technical issues across multiple technology platforms. Knowledge of Microsoft 365 administration and cloud-integrated services preferred. Strong verbal, written, organizational, and technical documentation skills. Ability to communicate technical concepts effectively to both technical and nontechnical audiences. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, staff, students, vendors, and colleagues. Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion. Senior Systems Administrator Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field preferred. Relevant technical certifications may be considered in lieu of some educational requirements. Minimum of seven (7) years of progressively responsible experience in systems administration, enterprise infrastructure, endpoint engineering, virtualization, or related technical operations. Demonstrated experience leading enterprise technology initiatives and complex infrastructure projects. Experience supporting cloud and hybrid technology environments. Experience mentoring technical staff and serving as a senior escalation resource preferred. Advanced knowledge of enterprise systems administration, endpoint management, virtualization, automation, and cloud services. Advanced knowledge of Microsoft Active Directory, Microsoft Entra ID, Microsoft 365, identity management, and authentication technologies. Experience with scripting and automation technologies such as PowerShell, Bash, or equivalent tools. Knowledge of cybersecurity best practices, endpoint security controls, vulnerability remediation, and compliance standards. Experience with disaster recovery planning, business continuity initiatives, and infrastructure modernization projects. Ability to design, implement, and support enterprise technology solutions with minimal supervision. Strong leadership, project management, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Ability to provide technical leadership, mentoring, and guidance to technical staff. Ability to manage multiple priorities and projects in a dynamic environment. Excellent verbal, written, presentation, and documentation skills. Preferred Certifications Microsoft Certified Professional (MCP), Microsoft Certified: Azure Administrator Associate, or equivalent. Apple Certified Support Professional (ACSP) or JAMF certifications. VMware, Citrix, CompTIA Server+, Security+, or equivalent industry certifications. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity.\u00a0 Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), and three references and submitted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/192104 .\u00a0\u00a0Questions may be directed to Mark Fleming at mafleming@smcm.edu. Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/192111": {"title": "Director of Enterprise Applications and Integration Services", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Business and Finance: OIT Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland (the College) at Historic St. Mary\u2019s City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for the position of Director of Enterprise Applications and Integration Services. The Director of Enterprise Applications and Integration Services serves as the institutional leader responsible for the ongoing operation, support, optimization, governance, and strategic direction of enterprise administrative systems supporting Human Resources, Finance, Payroll, Student Administration, Financial Aid, Advancement, Institutional Research, and other administrative functions. The position oversees enterprise application services, cloud-based applications, Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) platforms, application integrations, data exchange processes, reporting services, vendor relationships, and related business systems. This position reports to the Associate Vice President and Chief Information Officer and is responsible for the strategic leadership, administration, governance, security, and operational support of the College\u2019s enterprise applications and integration services environment. The salary range for this position is $122,000 to $140,000, depending on qualifications and experience. The Director supervises enterprise application personnel, including the HR/Finance Cloud DBA, Student Cloud DBA, Business Analyst(s), and other assigned staff, and serves as the primary technology and operational leader for enterprise applications, cloud services, integrations, enterprise data services, and related technology solutions supporting the College. The position is responsible for ensuring enterprise systems, cloud applications, integrations, and associated business processes effectively support the mission, goals, and strategic objectives of the College while maintaining appropriate levels of security, compliance, reliability, performance, data protection, and operational effectiveness. The Director collaborates closely with Information Technology leadership, cybersecurity personnel, functional departments, vendors, consultants, and executive leadership to promote effective governance, secure operations, institutional data stewardship, and continuous improvement of enterprise technology services. Non-sectarian since its founding, St. Mary's College of Maryland, a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C., has been designated as Maryland's public honors college.\u00a0 Undergraduate and residential in nature, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1700, St. Mary's emphasizes excellence in teaching.\u00a0 The institution was awarded a chapter of Phi Beta Kappa in 1997.\u00a0 The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Bachelor's degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, Business Administration, Higher Education Administration, or a related field required. Master's degree preferred. Minimum of seven (7) years of progressively responsible experience supporting enterprise applications, enterprise systems, cloud-based technologies, administrative technologies, or related information technology services. Minimum of three (3) years of supervisory or management experience. Experience supporting enterprise administrative systems, ERP platforms, cloud-hosted applications, Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) solutions, or related enterprise technologies. Experience managing system integrations, APIs, data exchanges, middleware technologies, or related integration services. Experience with enterprise application security, identity and access management, governance processes, risk management, compliance activities, or audit remidiation efforts. Experience with project management, business process analysis, operational planning, vendor management, and enterprise technology governance. Experience with Workday, Anthology, Ellucian Banner or Colleague, Oracle PeopleSoft, or comparable enterprise ERP and administrative application platforms. Experience supporting enterprise reporting, analytics, data, governance, and institutional compliance requirements. Experience supporting enterprise integrations, APIs, middleware platforms, and secure data exchange services. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity.\u00a0 Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), statement of how the applicant\u2019s employment at the College will contribute to a culture of inclusion and campus diversity, and three references and submitted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/192111 .\u00a0 Questions may be directed to E. Jenell Sargent at 240-895-4331. Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/183215": {"title": "Development Research Coordinator", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Advancement: Development Location: St. Mary's City, MD 20686 St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary\u2019s City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for the position of Development Research Coordinator . The Development Research Coordinator is an integral member of Institutional Advancement\u2019s Development team who applies creative research techniques to provide high-level description and analysis on individuals, corporations, and foundations using a wide variety of biographical, organizational, anecdotal and financial sources. The position draws upon multiple resources to assess financial capacity, philanthropic tendencies, giving propensity, and connections with the College with the goal of generating new donations and fostering strategically important relationships with the College. The salary range is $54,000-$57,000, depending on qualifications and experience. The Development Research Coordinator is responsible for Raiser's Edge database functionality as it relates to prospect and donor management. The position has responsibility for implementing strategies to grow a dynamic prospect pipeline. The incumbent will prepare research and reports for prospect and donor strategy sessions with the Development team and will also be responsible for analysis and interpretation of portfolio performance. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. A bachelor's degree is required. A minimum of three (3) years of experience in prospect research, development, library research or related field. Proven experience in Internet-based research and CRM databases. Experience with Raiser\u2019s Edge is preferred. Ability to analyze and synthesize data from a wide variety of sources, and present the resulting information in clear, concise summaries. Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information. Exhibits strong computer, organizational/time management and communications skills and is detail-oriented. Understanding of the fundraising cycle and portfolio and moves management preferred. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity.\u00a0 Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), and three professional references and are being accepted online at: apply.interfolio.com/183215 .\u00a0 Questions may be directed to Sarah Miller Martin at slmillermartin@smcm.edu or 240-895-4282. Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer. Visit our website: www.smcm.edu/hr"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/184445": {"title": "Executive Director of Student Financial Services", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Admissions: Financial Aid Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary's College of Maryland, the 5 th ranked public liberal arts college and the first standalone public honors college in the U.S. is accepting application materials for the position of Executive Director of Student Financial Services. The salary for this position is $128,700 - $147,600, depending on skills and experience. The Executive Director of Student Financial Services (EDSFS) is newly created role designed to provide strategic leadership, policy direction, and operational oversight for Office of Student Financial Assistance and the Office of Student Accounts. Reporting to the Vice President of Enrollment Management and as a member of the Division of Enrollment Management leadership team, the inaugural EDSFS will play a central role in advancing the College\u2019s enrollment, net tuition revenue, and student success goals through the effective, compliant, and student-centered delivery of financial aid and student account services. The EDSFS serves as the College\u2019s chief Title IV compliance officer, Primary Federal Eligibility and Oversight Administrator, and Primary Destination Point Administrator (DPA) for or Title IV funds. This role requires balancing rigorous regulatory compliance with innovative, data-informed financial aid strategies that promote access, affordability, persistence, and timely degree completion while delivering a high-quality service experience for students and families. The Executive Director collaborates closely with leaders in Enrollment Management and across the College including Finance, the Registrar, Academic Affairs, Institutional Research to ensure integrated, mission-aligned financial and administrative support for a diverse student body, consistent with the College\u2019s identity as The National Public Honors College. St. Mary's College of Maryland, non-sectarian since its establishment as a living monument to the founding of the state of Maryland in 1840, is a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. Undergraduate and residential in nature, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1700, St. Mary's emphasizes excellence in teaching and experiential learning.\u00a0 The institution was awarded a chapter of Phi Beta Kappa in 1997.\u00a0 The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Bachelor's degree required; Master's degree is preferred. Five (5) to seven (7) years of progressive experience in financial aid and/or student accounts administration, preferably at the director or associate level. Three (3) to five (5) years of experience supervising professional and support staff. Expert knowledge of federal, state, and institutional financial aid regulations, cash management, and compliance requirements (including military and veteran benefits). Demonstrated experience with audits, responding to findings, and implementing corrective action plans. Strong knowledge of accounting principles, budgeting, and fiscal reporting. Proficiency with federal systems (Common Origination and Disbursement (COD), National Student Loan Data System (NSLDS), Student Aid Internet Gateway (SAIG), FAA Access, FSA Partner Connect, and the E-App) and enterprise student systems. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel and related productivity tools. Demonstrated ability to: Align financial aid strategy with enrollment and student success goals. Lead complex, compliance-driven operations. Build trust and collaboration across divisions. Communicate effectively with students, families, staff, and senior leadership. Strong commitment to access, equity, student advocacy, and the mission of St. Mary's College of Maryland as The National Public Honors College. Demonstrated success leading, developing, and mentoring diverse teams. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity.\u00a0 Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), diversity statement, and three references and submitted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/184445 .\u00a0 Questions may be directed to David Hautanen at dlhautanen@smcm.edu. Review of resumes will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Visit our website: https://www.smcm.edu/"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/194165": {"title": "Dispatcher", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Student Affairs: Public Safety Location: St. Mary's City, Maryland St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary's City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for the position of Dispatcher in the Office of Public Safety.\u00a0 General duties include operation of radio communications equipment, dispatching routine and emergency calls for service, handling requests for service from the campus community and the general public, and acting as liaison with County and State Emergency Services. Must be able to work a rotating shift schedule or fixed shift schedule as determined by operational needs.\u00a0 Must be able to work weekends and holidays. Along with the ability to handle a fast-paced environment, the successful candidate must have a high school diploma or GED equivalency, six months of related experience, familiarity with basic data entry, excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to work and communicate well with students.\u00a0 Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered.\u00a0 Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. This is a full-time entry level position with an annual salary of $35,570, plus benefits. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Ability to handle a fast paced environment. Must have a high school diploma or GED equivalency. At least six months of related experience, familiarity with basic data entry. Excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to work and communicate well with students. Working hours are varied on a 24-hour per day basis. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland (www.smcm.edu) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity.\u00a0 Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), and three references and submitted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/194165 . Questions may be directed to OA Gunther in the Office of Public Safety at angunther@smcm.edu. Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/189543": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Anthropology", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Anthroplogy Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland (SMCM) is accepting applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Anthropology with a focus in Biological Anthropology whose work will also contribute to the College\u2019s new Public Health major.\u00a0 Candidates who value the scholar\u2013teacher model of the liberal arts are encouraged to apply. Teaching responsibilities entail three classes per semester for a total of six per year, including a four-field \u201cIntroduction to Anthropology,\u201d \u201cBiological Anthropology,\u201d and public health courses, including \u201cIntroduction to Public Health\u201d and \u201cHuman Anatomy for Public Health.\u201d Topics courses in the candidate\u2019s areas of expertise are welcome. We especially seek candidates whose elective courses can support interest in global health and wellness, medical anthropology, or the application of anthropology to public health. In addition to an active research agenda, competitive candidates should be able to demonstrate interest in and ability to offer hands-on student research opportunities and learning experiences that take advantage of our location. We especially value course-based research opportunities and other high-impact practices you can bring to SMCM. The salary range for this position is $75,000 to $80,000, depending on qualifications and experience. When extending an offer of employment, the College considers factors including, but not limited to, education and training, work experience, internal peer equity, and organizational considerations. This salary range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate at the time of posting. Non-sectarian since its founding, St. Mary's College of Maryland, a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in St. Mary\u2019s City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C., has been designated as Maryland's public honors college.\u00a0 With selective admissions policies, academically talented students, and a rigorous curriculum, we offer a small college experience similar to that found at exceptional private colleges. St. Mary\u2019s faculty benefit from a comprehensive program of support for scholarship, research, travel, and curriculum development, including course releases for pre-tenure faculty and leaves for tenured faculty.\u00a0 The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and by our proximity to Washington, D.C. and Baltimore. Qualifications include a Ph.D. in Anthropology at the time of hire, with a record of high-quality teaching and research. A commitment to attracting and retaining students from underrepresented groups is valued. St. Mary\u2019s College (www.smcm.edu) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae (include email address), statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research interests, and evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available). In support of inclusive hiring practices, for all SMCM faculty searches initiated after February 15, 2023, the College will also request three professional references (rather than letters of recommendation) at the time of application. Of these three references, at least one reference should speak to the candidate's disciplinary expertise and at least one should have seen the candidate deliver or design classroom instruction. References will be contacted only for candidates who advance to finalist interviews. Applications are being accepted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/189543 . Questions may be directed to: Liza Gijanto at lgijanto@smcm.edu. Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Visit our website: www.smcm.edu/hr"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/184989": {"title": "Assistant Field Hockey Coach/Assistant Athletic Communications Director", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Athletics and Recreation Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary\u2019s City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for the position of Assistant Field Hockey Coach/Assistant Athletic Communications Director .\u00a0 Duties for the Assistant Field Hockey position include assisting in all areas of coaching the field hockey team including, but not limited to, recruiting, organizing and planning practices and game strategies, and fund raising.\u00a0 The secondary duties for Assistant Athletic Communications Director will include writing and distributing press releases, writing post game stories, preparing game notes/programs, managing game-day statistic responsibilities, overseeing the athletic department\u2019s social media outlets and supervising web video production. This position reports to the Head Field hockey Coach and the Director of Athletic Communications. The annual salary for this position is $44,327. Non-sectarian since its founding, St. Mary's College of Maryland, a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C., has been designated as Maryland's public honors college.\u00a0 Undergraduate and residential in nature, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600, St. Mary's emphasizes excellence in teaching.\u00a0 The institution was awarded a chapter of Phi Beta Kappa in 1997.\u00a0 The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Bachelor\u2019s degree, and knowledge of NCAA and United East Conference rules and regulations. Experience in collegiate coaching is preferred. Must possess a valid driver\u2019s license. Ability to travel and work nights and weekends required. Ability to lift approximately thirty (30) pounds. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College (www.smcm.edu) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. \u00a0We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity.\u00a0 Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), statement of how the applicant\u2019s employment at the College will contribute to a culture of inclusion and campus diversity, and three references and submitted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/184989 . Questions may be directed to Allyson Osborne at agosborne@smcm.edu. Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Visit our website: https://www.smcm.edu/"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/179973": {"title": "Groundskeeper I", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Business and Finance: Physical Plant Location: St. Mary's City, MD 20686 St. Mary's College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary's City is accepting applications for the position of Groundskeeper I .\u00a0 Employees will be required to perform heavy lifting, work in inclement weather, do minor repairs to equipment and operate all tools and equipment associated with grounds. Employees in this position are \"essential\" and will be required to work after hours to remove snow and ice in emergency situations and other overtime requirements. Employees must be dependable and punctual. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Two years\u2019 experience in the field of grounds maintenance. Must possess a valid Maryland driver\u2019s license. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Annual salary is $35,570 with an excellent benefits package that includes but is not limited to 18 paid holidays, 12 days vacation, 3 paid personal days, health benefit and prescription plans, pension plan, and tuition waiver plan. View position description . St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Please submit a cover letter, resume, and three references preferably online at: apply.interfolio.com/179973 . Applications and position descriptions for this position are linked in this ad or may be obtained from Joyce Goodwine, Office of Physical Plant, St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland, 47645 College Drive, St. Mary's City, Maryland 20686-3001; or email jcgoodwine@smcm.edu. Review of all applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. St. Mary's College of Maryland is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer. Visit our website: www.smcm.edu/hr"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/179974": {"title": "Caretaker I (Housekeeper)", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Business and Finance: Physical Plant Location: St. Mary's City, Maryland St. Mary's College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary's City is accepting applications for several positions of Caretaker I (Housekeeper). Caretaker I is a skilled position in housekeeping and minor maintenance trades.\u00a0 Responsibilities include vacuuming, moving furniture, stripping and waxing floors, setting up for College functions, changing light bulbs, and assistance in grounds if needed.\u00a0 Employees must be able to follow oral and written instructions and regularly lift heavy items such as furniture or equipment.\u00a0 Overtime/weekend work will be required.\u00a0 Must be dependable and punctual.\u00a0\u00a0 Previous custodial experience or training is a plus. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Two years experience in cleaning or housekeeping field. Must possess a valid Maryland driver\u2019s license. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Annual salary is $35,570 with an excellent benefits package that includes but is not limited to 18 paid holidays, 12 days vacation, 3 paid personal days, health benefit and prescription plans, pension plan, and tuition waiver plan. St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Please submit a cover letter, resume, and three references preferably online at: apply.interfolio.com/179974 .\u00a0 Questions may be directed to Joyce Goodwine at 240-895-4287. Applications and position descriptions may also be obtained from Physical Plant at St. Mary's College of Maryland, 47645 College Drive, St. Mary's City, Maryland 20686-3001. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled.\u00a0 St. Mary's College of Maryland is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer. Visit our website: www.smcm.edu/hr"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/185954": {"title": "Assistant Supervisor of the Mailroom", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Business and Finance: Physical Plant Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary\u2019s City is accepting resumes for the position of\u00a0Assistant Supervisor of the Mailroom. This position supervises the receiving and distribution of mail, supplies, inventory, and central stores supplies.\u00a0 Person in this position reports to and takes instruction from the Office Manager in the Physical Plant or any other designated higher Physical Plant Staff member.\u00a0 Person will also provide some oversight of warehouse facility for janitorial, office and general supplies, office furniture and equipment and conducting a central stores operation with inventory control.\u00a0 Employee must be punctual and dependable. The annual salary range is $35,570-$38,000, depending on qualifications and experience. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public honors College, is in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for instate and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. High School diploma or GED equivalent. Experience in inventory, mailroom, record keeping, shipping or receiving a plus but not required. Must possess a valid Maryland driver's license. Must have the ability to operate computers and a general knowledge of some software applications. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should be submitted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/185954 and include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), and three references. Questions may be directed to Bradley Newkirk at bdnewkirk@smcm.edu or 240-895-4287. Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/193032": {"title": "Lab Technician (Biology)", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Biology Location: St. Mary's City, MD The Department of Biology at St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland is accepting applications for a part-time position of Lab Technician, beginning September 2026. The position is funded by an NIH grant. The project will study thyroid hormone signaling and lead exposure in the developing brain using Xenopus laevis as a model system. The hourly rate for this position is $22. Non-sectarian since its founding, St. Mary's College of Maryland, a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C., has been designated as Maryland's public honors college. With selective admissions policies, academically talented students, and a rigorous curriculum, we offer a small college experience similar to that found at exceptional private colleges. St. Mary\u2019s faculty benefit from a comprehensive program of support for scholarship, research, travel, and curriculum development, including course releases for pre-tenure faculty and leaves for tenured faculty. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and by our proximity to Washington, D.C. and Baltimore. Applicants must have a bachelor\u2019s degree in Biology or related field. Prior lab experience is preferred but not required. The successful candidate will have the following characteristics: Attention to detail and reliability Comfort working independently is very important Prior lab experience preferred but not required Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College (www.smcm.edu) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include a cover letter, a resume or curriculum vitae, and names of three references. References will be contacted only for candidates who advance to finalist interviews. Applications are being accepted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/193032 .\u00a0 Questions may be directed to Dr. Thompson at ckthompson@smcm.edu."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/188798": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty AY 26-27", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Academic Affairs Location: Saint Marys City, MD, United States St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland is accepting\u00a0applications for the contingent\u00a0position of Adjunct Faculty . Adjunct faculty are temporary, ad hoc, non-tenure-track teaching positions, hired to teach specific courses as needed by the College. Application materials are held on file for one academic year, after which applicants may resubmit their applications.\u00a0 These contingent positions pay a salary of $4,500 to teach one 4 credit course, with no benefits provided. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Qualifications will vary according to position. Minimum requirements include an advanced post-graduate degree, with preference for terminal post-graduate degree, in related field of study. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include a cover letter (within the cover letter, applicants are requested to speak to ways in which their teaching will contribute to a culture of inclusion and campus diversity), curriculum vitae (including email address) ; and evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available). In support of inclusive hiring practices, the College will also request three professional references (rather than letters of recommendation) at the time of application. Of these three references, at least one referee should speak to the candidate's disciplinary expertise and at least one should have seen the candidate deliver or design classroom instruction. References will be contacted only for candidates who advance to finalist interviews. Applications are being accepted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/188798 . Questions may be directed to Dr. Katherine Gantz, Vice President for Academic Affairs and Dean of Faculty, klgantz@smcm.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/192116": {"title": "Finance & Accounting Operations Manager", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Business and Finance Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary\u2019s City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for the position of Finance & Accounting Operations Manager. Under the direction of the Assistant Vice President of Business/Controller, the Finance & Accounting Operations Manager oversees the business affairs and budget functions of the College.\u00a0 The incumbent collects, maintains, and analyzes financial data to support business objectives and sound fiscal management; assists with the preparation of financial reports, metrics, projections, budgets, year-end closing activities, and other financial analyses, while maintaining accurate and timely financial dashboards for management insight. The Finance & Accounting Operations Manager ensures financial reporting, operations, and transactions comply with organizational policies, regulatory requirements, financial standards, internal controls, and applicable GASB requirements; supports the accuracy, integrity, and timely reporting of the College\u2019s financial activities and contributes to effective capital and operating budget management and overall fiscal stewardship. Required skills include ability to self-direct, perform quantitative analyses, data query, analysis, and manipulation, and excel at verbal and written communication. The salary range is $75,000 - $82,000 with a contract end date of March 31, 2028 St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Bachelor\u2019s degree in accounting or business administration. Advanced degree preferred. Certified Public Accountant (CPA) designation is beneficial. Five (5) years\u2019 accounting, fiscal or budgetary experience working in a non-profit organization; college or university setting preferred. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), and three references and submitted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/192116 . Questions may be directed to Mary Grube at mkgrube@smcm.edu Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/193033": {"title": "Workday Change Manager", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Business and Finance Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary\u2019s City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for the position of Workday Change Manager.\u00a0\u00a0The Change Manager leads and coordinates organizational change activities supporting the Workday implementation. The role focuses on preparing faculty, staff, leaders, and other impacted stakeholders for changes to business processes, roles, responsibilities, and ways of working resulting from Workday. Working closely with the Project Manager, functional and technical leads, Training Lead, Communications & Marketing, and the implementation partner, the Change Manager develops and executes a coordinated change approach that supports awareness, engagement, readiness, adoption, and transition to the new system. The salary range for this position is $78,000 to $92,000, depending on qualifications and experience. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. 5+ years of change management experience, including experience supporting ERP, HCM, financial system, or Workday-related implementations. Experience supporting changes affecting multiple functional areas such as Finance, Human Resources, Payroll, and/or Student administration. Ability to translate complex system and process changes into clear, practical messages for nontechnical audiences. Strong stakeholder engagement, facilitation, communication, and relationship-management skills, including experience working with senior leaders and cross-functional stakeholders. Experience conducting stakeholder, change-impact, and organizational-readiness assessments. Ability to work effectively with executives, project leadership, functional teams, technical teams, communications professionals, and implementation partners. Strong planning and organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple change activities against an integrated project schedule. Experience in higher education strongly preferred; direct Workday HCM, Payroll, Financials, and/or Student implementation experience is preferred. Familiarity with established change-management approaches such as ADKAR/Prosci is preferred; practical application is more important than adherence to a particular methodology. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include: Cover letter Resume (including email address) Cotnact information for three (3) professional references Applications can be submitted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/193033 . Questions may be directed to Wanda Fenwick at wmfenwick@smcm.edu."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/170440": {"title": "Audio Visual Technician (part-time, contingent)", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Business and Finance: OIT Location: Saint Marys City, MD, United States St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary\u2019s City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for two part-time positions of Audio Visual Technician (part-time, contingent). These part-time contingent positions report to the Director of Instructional Systems and Support and is responsible for audio visual support for events, and also provides Tiers 1 and 2 support of the operations of technologies and media in classrooms. Must be well organized and possess good communications and technology skills.\u00a0 Handles confidential and sensitive issues. These are part-time (approximately 30 hours per week) contingent positions with an hourly pay rate of $35, depending on qualifications and experience. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. High School diploma or equivalent required. Bachelor\u2019s degree preferred. A minimum of one year of experience in a media-related or IT field. Must have a working knowledge of both Mac and PC operating systems and classroom media including computer, audio, and video systems. Strong verbal, written, analytical, interpersonal, and organizational skills are a must. Must be able to lift at least 50 pounds. Must possess a valid driver\u2019s license. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. View position description . St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity.\u00a0 Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), and three references and submitted online at: apply.interfolio.com/170440 .\u00a0 Questions may be directed to Jennifer Falkowski at jafalkowski@smcm.edu . Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer. Visit our website: www.smcm.edu/hr"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/170997": {"title": "Desktop Deployment Technician and Asset Manager", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Business and Finance: OIT Location: St. Mary's City, Maryland 20686 St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary\u2019s City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for the part-time, temporary contingent position of Desktop Deployment Technician and Asset Manager . The Desktop Deployment Technician and Asset Manager plays a key role in supporting the institution\u2019s technology infrastructure by managing the lifecycle of desktop systems and peripheral assets. This mid-level position is responsible for the imaging, deployment, maintenance, and decommissioning of computer systems, as well as overseeing the IT asset inventory to ensure accurate tracking, compliance, and optimal allocation of resources. This individual will collaborate closely with IT support staff, faculty, and administrative departments to maintain a consistent, secure, and well-documented computing environment. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Associate\u2019s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or related field (or equivalent professional experience), bachelor\u2019s degree preferred. Two or more years of experience in desktop deployment, technical support, or IT asset management. Proficiency with Windows OS imaging and deployment tools. Familiarity with IT inventory tracking software and asset tagging practices. Strong problem-solving and organizational skills. Excellent interpersonal communication and customer service skills. Ability to lift and move computer equipment weighing at least 50 pounds. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. View position description . The hourly pay rate is $35, depending on qualifications and experience. St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity.\u00a0 Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), and three references and submitted online at: apply.interfolio.com/170997 .\u00a0 Questions may be directed to\u00a0 E. Jenell Sargent, AVP/CIO of Information Technology\u00a0 at ejsargent@smcm.edu . Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer. Visit our website: www.smcm.edu/hr"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/171151": {"title": "Group Fitness Instructors (Part-time)", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Athletics and Recreation Location: St. Mary's City, MD 20686 St. Mary's College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary's City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for several part-time contingent positions as Group Fitness Instructors. Responsibilities include teaching land or water-based group exercise classes in a safe and effective manner for all skill levels.\u00a0 Instructors will also assist with special events and workshops related to the group exercise area.\u00a0 These positions are contingent upon program development and interest. \u00a0These are part-time contingent positions with no benefits provided. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Demonstrated group exercise knowledge, experience, and effectiveness. Current instructor certification from ACE, ACSM, AFAA, NDEITA or other nationally recognized group exercise certification preferred. First Aid and CPR/AED certified by the American Red Cross or equivalent organization. Group Fitness Instructors are responsible for their own class itineraries and for providing a safe and healthy workout environment. Ability to lift at least thirty (30) pounds. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. The hourly pay rate is $30, depending on qualifications and experience. View position description . St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity.\u00a0 Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), and three references and submitted online at apply.interfolio.com/171151 .\u00a0 \u00a0Questions may be directed to Tom Fisher at twfisher@smcm.edu Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 St. Mary's College of Maryland is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer. Visit our website: www.smcm.edu/hr"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/184278": {"title": "Assistant Women's Lacrosse Goalkeeper Coach", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Athletics and Recreation Location: St. Mary's City, MD 20686 St. Mary's College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary's City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for the part-time contingent position of Assistant Women\u2019s Lacrosse Goalkeeper Coach. The salary for this position is $2000 per year. Responsibilities include serving as a goalkeeper coach in a competitive NCAA Division III women\u2019s lacrosse program.\u00a0 Duties for the Assistant Women\u2019s Lacrosse position include assisting in all areas of coaching the women\u2019s lacrosse team including, but not limited to, recruiting, organizing and planning practices and game strategies. Non-sectarian since its founding, St. Mary's College of Maryland, a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C., has been designated as Maryland's public honors college.\u00a0 Undergraduate and residential in nature, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600, St. Mary's emphasizes excellence in teaching.\u00a0 The institution was awarded a chapter of Phi Beta Kappa in 1997.\u00a0 The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Bachelor\u2019s degree required and knowledge of NCAA and United East Conference rules and regulations. Experience in collegiate coaching is preferred. Must possess a valid driver\u2019s license. Ability to travel, work nights and weekends, and lift approximately thirty (30) pounds is required. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity.\u00a0 Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), and three references and submitted online at: https://apply.interfolio.com/184278 .\u00a0 Questions may be directed to Maddie Heck at meheck@smcm.edu. Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Visit our website: www.smcm.edu"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/195522": {"title": "Assistant Track & Field Coach for Sprints and Jumps", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Athletics and Recreation Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary's College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary's City is accepting resumes for the part-time position of Assistant Track & Field Coach: overseeing sprints and jumps. The Assistant Track & Field Coach is responsible for assistaning in the management of all phases of highly competitive NCAA Division III Track & Field programs, which includes recruitment of qualified student-athletes; coaching of assigned events during practice and compeition for men's and women's programs; administration, organization, and evaluation of all aspects of the program; and adherence to all NCAA Division III, conference and institutional policies and procedures. The hourly rate for this position is $15.00. Non-secretarian since its founding, St. Mary's College of Maryland, a public Carnegie Baccalaureate, Arts and Sciences institution located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington D.C., has been designated as Maryland's public honors college. Undergraduate and residential in nature, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600, St. Mary's emphasizes excellence in teaching. The institution was awarded a chapter of Phi Beta Kappa in 1997. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree Knowledge of NCAA and UEC rules and regulations Must possess a valid driver's licence Ability to lift approximately 30 pounds Ability to travel Ability to work nights and weekends Preferred Qualifications Experience in collegiate coaching and Certified Level One by the USATF or USTFCCC Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary's College (www.smcm.edu) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences, and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should be submitted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/195522 and include: Cover letter Resume Three (3) references Questions may be directed to Reava Potter, Director of Cross Country and Track & Field, at rnpotter@smcm.edu. Review of resumes will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/163828": {"title": "Professional Pathways Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Student Affairs: Career Development Center Location: Saint Marys City, MD, United States St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary\u2019s City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for several contingent positions of Professional Pathways Adjunct Instructor. This is an applicant pool for part time, temporary instructors. Instructors will facilitate self-discovery and career exploration; goal setting and informed decision making; soft skills and effective oral and written communication. Instructors may be considered for any course within the Professional Pathways sequence, including the Career & Network Navigation courses and the Honors College Externship course. These are part-time contingent positions with no benefits provided and an hourly pay of $25. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Master\u2019s degree, prior teaching experience and understanding of identity development theory and career development theory preferred. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from candidates who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including email address), and three references, and submitted online at apply.interfolio.com/ Questions may be directed to Darah Schillinger at daschillinger@smcm.edu . Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled.\u00a0 St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer. Visit our website: www.smcm.edu/hr"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/195326": {"title": "Records Management Specialist", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Academic Affairs: Registrar Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary's College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary's city is seeking qualified candidates for the position of Records Management Specialist. As a key member of the Office of the Registrar, the Records Management Specialist provides critical analytical support and data review during our ongoing transition to a new student information system (SIS). Key responsibilities include managing academic data clean-up in Anthology, training and supporting academic staff on SIS data and the Stellic platform, and overseeing the annual update of the college catalog via Modern Campus. Additionally, this role assists with degree certifications, class scheduling, and daily office operations\u2014such as processing transcripts, entering grades, updating course offerings, and managing administrative forms. The salary range for this position is $49,000 to $51,000, commensurate with qualifications and experience. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Education: Bachelor's preferred; Associates degree required. Experience: Two (2) to four (4) years administrative experience in a Registrar's office preferred; at least one (1) year of other administrative experience in data review and management in higher education required. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. Application can be submitted at https://apply.interfolio.com/195326 and should include the following: Cover letter Resume Three (3) professional references Questions may be directed to Nick Tulley, Registrar, at nbtulley@smcm.edu. Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/192562": {"title": "Bus Driver", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Business and Finance: Physical Plant Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland at Historic St. Mary\u2019s City is accepting r\u00e9sum\u00e9s for the part-time contingent position of Bus Driver. This position involves independent judgment and will be responsible for transporting students/faculty/staff to and from campus and extracurricular events, following a scheduled route, and ensuring the safety of all passengers. This is a part-time position with a variable schedule that will include some evenings and weekends. The pay for this part-time position is $25 to $32 hourly, based on experience.\u00a0 This position does not supervise other employees. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Must have a high school diploma or GED equivalent and at least three years of driving experience. Must have a good knowledge of concepts, practices, and procedures within the transportation industry, including DOT regulations and required to possess a current DOT Medical Card. Must not be disqualified to drive a commercial motor vehicle as described in CFR 391 and must possess a current CDL A or B license with Passenger and Airbrake Endorsement. The successful applicant will be subject to a criminal background check and random substance abuse testing. Must possess a valid Maryland driver\u2019s license, must have excellent driving history, and be available during non-traditional working hours. Must have or be able to obtain CPR and First Aid Certifications. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission.\u00a0 We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences, and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity.\u00a0 Application materials should include a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 (including e-mail address), and three references and submitted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/192562 . Questions may be directed to Brad Newkirk at bdnewkirk@smcm.edu . Review of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/187609": {"title": "Accompanist for Music", "description": "Department: St. Mary's College of Maryland: Advancement: Performing Arts Location: St. Mary's City, MD St. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland is accepting applications for the contingent position of Accompanist for Music . Accompanists are temporary, ad hoc, non-tenure-track positions, hired to accompany specific activities for the Music program as needed.\u00a0 These may include lessons, rehearsals, and recitals. Application materials are held on file for one academic year, after which applicants may resubmit their applications. These contingent positions pay $70 per hour, depending on qualifications and experience, with no benefits provided. St. Mary's College of Maryland, the National Public Honors College, is located in Historic St. Mary's City, 70 miles southeast of Washington, D.C. St. Mary\u2019s College is one of the nation\u2019s best public liberal arts colleges \u2013 ranked near the top in U.S. News & World Report and a Best Value for in-state and out-of-state students. Non-sectarian since its founding, the college with its scenic waterfront campus is primarily undergraduate and residential, with a diverse coeducational student body numbering approximately 1600. The up-to-date curriculum is designed for today\u2019s students who want an active, hands-on education led by professors who are committed teachers and experts in their fields. The quality of life is enhanced by the recreational opportunities of the Chesapeake region and close proximity to the amenities of Washington D.C., Baltimore and Richmond. Qualifications will vary according to position; minimum requirements include exceptional sightreading skills and ability to learn music quickly, strong knowledge of standard instrumental repertoire, excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Any combination of acceptable education and experience, which has provided the necessary knowledge and skills to fulfill the requirements of this position, may be considered. Employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. St. Mary\u2019s College ( www.smcm.edu ) embodies diversity and inclusion in its mission. We create an environment that recognizes the value of individual and group differences, and we encourage inquiries from applicants who will contribute to our cultural and ethnic diversity. \\ Application materials should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae (including email address), and three professional references. References will be contacted only for candidates who advance to finalist interviews. Applications are being accepted online at https://apply.interfolio.com/187609 . Questions may be directed to Leigh Ann Hinton, Operations Coordinator for Music, at lahinton@smcm.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled."}}, "rows": {"https://apply.interfolio.com/190337": {"school_id": 606, "posting_url": "https://apply.interfolio.com/190337", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor of Psychology", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Psychology", "area_key_words": "Psychology", "deadline_of_application": "September 1, 2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/190488": {"school_id": 606, "posting_url": "https://apply.interfolio.com/190488", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor and Internship Coordinator in Counseling and Clinical Psychology", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Counseling and Clinical Psychology; Clinical Psychology program", "deadline_of_application": "September 1, 2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/190323": {"school_id": 606, "posting_url": "https://apply.interfolio.com/190323", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor of De